  "uprn": "100021553005",
  "decision_date": "31/01/2019",
  "description": "Variation of Condition 3 (approved plans) to enable changes to internal layout following planning permission 00676/71C/P7 dated 2/7/2013  for demolition of existing Chalet Bungalow and erection of a three storey building and pitched roof  to provide four two-bedroom flats, two one-bedroom flats and one studio flat with associated parking/turning area and the construction of vehicle access",
  "site_name": "71c",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "10/12/2018",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW3 4DH",
  "street_name": "Lampton Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "30/01/2022",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Location Plan; Statement; I/434-110; I/111; I/112; Received 15/10/2018.) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - The refuse storage provision shall be provided out and permanently retained thereafter in accordance with the details approved by planning permission 00676/71C/P7(2-16) on 30 June 2016 within three months of the date of this decision.",
    "Condition : 5 - The hard and soft landscape works shall be carried out and kept in accordance with the details approved by planning permission 00676/71C/P7(2-16) on 30 June 2016 within three months of the date of this decision.",
    "Condition : 6 - The means of pedestrian and vehicular access shall be constructed in accordance with the approved plans within the planning application 00676/71C/P7 within three months of this decision.",
    "Condition : 7 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays and maintained as such.",
    "Condition : 8 - The car parking accommodation shown on the approved plans within the planning application 00676/71C/P7 shall be provided at all times and it shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 9 - The evidence (e.g. photographs and copies of installation contracts) shall be submitted and approved within three months of this decision to the Local Planning Authority to demonstrate that the development has been carried out in accordance with the approved details 00676/71C/P7(2i-16i) on 30 June 2016.",
    "Condition : 10 - Within three months of this decision, a Code for Sustainable Homes Interim (Design Stage) Certificate, issued by the Building Research Establishment (BRE) or equivalent licensing organisation, must be submitted for each dwelling to the Local Planning Authority to show that a minimum Level 3 rating will be achieved.",
    "Condition : 11 - Within three months of this decision, a Code for Sustainable Homes Final (Post-Construction) Certificate, issued by the BRE equivalent licensing organisation, must be submitted for each dwelling to the Local Planning Authority to demonstrate that Level 3 has been achieved. All the measures integrated shall be retained for as long as the development is in existence.",
    "Condition : 12 - Within three months of this decision, evidence (e.g. photographs and copies of installation contracts) shall have been submitted to the Local Planning Authority to demonstrate that the development has been carried out in accordance with the approved details 00676/71C/P7(2i-16i) on 30 June 2016."
  ],
